cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "The Book That Plays Back"
message: "If you use or cite this work, please cite it as below."
type: book
authors:
  - family-names: "Correia"
    given-names: "Arthur Endlein"
abstract: >-
  A print gamebook you play against: make a move, turn to the page it
  sends you to, and the book has already replied. Every answer was
  precomputed by minimax (with a trap-maximising tie-break). Five games
  inside (tic-tac-toe, hexapawn, notakto, nim, twenty-one), a
  history-of-machines timeline along the page foot, essays on the MENACE
  matchbox learning machine and the Sprague-Grundy theorem, a glossary,
  a cut-out matchbox kit, and a certificate. Generated deterministically
  by a short Python program (book.py) from random seed 43, typeset with
  Forme and compiled with XeLaTeX; rebuilds byte-identically from source.
keywords:
  - combinatorial game theory
  - tic-tac-toe
  - nim
  - minimax
  - Sprague-Grundy
  - generative book
  - reproducible
  - gamebook
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
